# PharmChain: Experimental Artifacts

**Paper:** PharmChain: A Blockchain-Enabled Framework for Pharmaceutical Supply Chain Transparency and Counterfeit Medicine Prevention

**Status:** Manuscript under review. Full artifact package will be publicly released upon acceptance.

---

## Repository Structure

```
pharmchain_artifacts/
├── chaincode/                  # Smart contracts (Go, Hyperledger Fabric v2.4)
│   ├── drugregistration.go     # DrugRegistration smart contract
│   ├── custodytransfer.go      # CustodyTransfer smart contract
│   └── counterfeitatert.go     # CounterfeitAlert smart contract
├── network_config/             # Hyperledger Fabric network configuration
│   ├── configtx.yaml           # Network channel and policy config
│   └── crypto-config.yaml      # Cryptographic material config
├── verification/               # Formal verification files
│   ├── drugasset.smv           # NuSMV model file (smart contract FSM)
│   └── hpoa_consensus.tla      # TLA+ specification (HPoA consensus protocol)
├── benchmark/                  # Hyperledger Caliper benchmark config
│   └── caliper_config.yaml     # Benchmark workload configuration
├── dataset/                    # Synthetic dataset generator
│   └── dataset_generator.py    # Python generator (seed=42, 50,000 transactions)
└── results/                    # Raw experimental results
    └── raw_results.csv         # 10 independent trial results
```

---

## System Requirements

- Hyperledger Fabric v2.4
- Go 1.18+
- Python 3.8+
- NuSMV v2.6
- TLA+ Toolbox with TLC Model Checker
- Hyperledger Caliper v0.5

---

## Experimental Configuration

| Parameter | Value |
|-----------|-------|
| Block size | 100 transactions |
| Block timeout | 1 second |
| Transaction payload | 512 bytes |
| Tier 2 validators | 4 (m=4, f=1) |
| Tier 3 endorsers | 1 |
| Independent trials | 10 |
| Counterfeit injection rate | 15% (7,500 / 50,000) |
| IoT sampling interval | 5 seconds |
| Random seed | 42 |

---

## Reproducibility

All results reported in the manuscript can be reproduced using these artifacts under identical configuration. Any deviation from reported values should be filed as a GitHub issue.

